---
/**
 * The shared warmup pool is a cloud feature: a single self-hosted instance
 * starts with an empty pool. Shown wherever a reader might assume self-hosting
 * brings a working pool with it.
 */
import Icon from './Icon.astro';

interface Props {
  class?: string;
  /** Show the waitlist link (default true). */
  showWaitlist?: boolean;
}
const { class: className = '', showWaitlist = true } = Astro.props;
---
<aside class={`rounded-[6px] bg-white p-6 ring-1 ring-slate-200 md:p-7 ${className}`}>
  <div class="text-[15px] font-medium text-slate-900">Self-hosting and the warmup pool</div>
  <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-[1.65] text-slate-600">
    The shared warmup pool runs on Warmbly Cloud, because a pool only works once enough vetted mailboxes are writing to each other. Self-hosted instances connect to the same pool, and the same rules keep its quality up wherever an instance runs.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-[1.65] text-slate-600">
    Self-hosting is free. When Warmbly Cloud launches, link your instance from Settings and we warm up to 10 of your mailboxes at no cost, or as many as you like for $15 a month. Sending, sequences, the inbox, the CRM, tracking and the API all stay on your own servers.
  </p>
  {showWaitlist && (
    <a href="https://app.warmbly.com" class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[14px] font-medium text-slate-900 hover:text-slate-600">
      Join the cloud waitlist
      <Icon name="arrowRight" size={12} />
    </a>
  )}
</aside>
